    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "294a234f_45ee62a4",
        "filename": "include/core/SkColorPriv.h",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 153,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-20T16:47:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is essentially an inlined version of SkAlphaMulQ, up to the point where we\u0027d combine `rb` and `ag`. Then, rather than do that (because we\u0027re going to have to pick them apart again...)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 151,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 153,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "9de8aeb44b449e3467153e1374f1e6edec31283f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "91d78c67_3028e236",
        "filename": "include/core/SkColorPriv.h",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 156,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-20T16:47:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "... we do the addition to `src` while things are still split into channel pairs. This prevents the overflow into adjacent channels. So we now have the even and odd channel sums, with a possible overflow bit spilling into the (otherwise zero\u0027d) space between.\n\nLuckily, the math is such that alpha can\u0027t overflow (and it\u0027s in the highest bits).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 155,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 156,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "9de8aeb44b449e3467153e1374f1e6edec31283f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "938a547a_f8c36a36",
        "filename": "include/core/SkColorPriv.h",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 163,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-20T16:47:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We do saturating adds of each color channel, then mask all the results together.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 159,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 163,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "9de8aeb44b449e3467153e1374f1e6edec31283f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "97c69544_b9783ae0",
        "filename": "include/core/SkColorPriv.h",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 163,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-20T17:06:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Once upon a time, I would have said this should be done branchless by using the \"overflow bit\" to create the mask. As things are though, the conditional moves will probably be almost always perfectly predicted, since this doesn\u0027t often overflow. Anyhow, something to consider, I suppose.",
      "parentUuid": "938a547a_f8c36a36",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 159,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 163,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "9de8aeb44b449e3467153e1374f1e6edec31283f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
